# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate declares a reference mode occupation; an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gate rotates the single-particle basis. Placed back to back, the two gates prepare a *Slater determinant*; the modes start in the reference determinant and are then rotated into the target orbitals. The [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate captures that composition, and because it carries the reference occupation, transpiling it can use the rectangular [`givens_decomposition_slater()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/linalg-givens-decomposition-slater#qiskit_fermions.linalg.givens_decomposition_slater \"qiskit_fermions.linalg.givens_decomposition_slater\"), which realizes only the *occupied* orbitals, instead of the full square decomposition an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") alone requires. That is a strictly cheaper synthesis (see the payoff at the end of this guide).\n"
msgstr "Uma porta [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") declara uma ocupação de modos de referência; uma porta [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gira a base de uma partícula. Colocadas em sequência, as duas portas preparam um *determinante de Slater*; os modos começam no determinante de referência e são então girados para os orbitais de destino. A porta [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") captura essa composição e, como carrega a ocupação de referência, transpilá-la pode usar a [`givens_decomposition_slater()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/linalg-givens-decomposition-slater#qiskit_fermions.linalg.givens_decomposition_slater \"qiskit_fermions.linalg.givens_decomposition_slater\") retangular, que realiza apenas os orbitais *ocupados*, em vez da decomposição quadrada completa que uma [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") sozinha exige. Essa é uma síntese estritamente mais barata (veja o ganho no final deste guia).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") transpiler pass detects the [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\")-then-[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") pattern in a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") and rewrites it into [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gates, so a later synthesis stage picks up the reduced decomposition automatically. Under simulation, the rewrite is a no-op on the state: [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") is *validate-then-rotate* (it validates the reference occupation and then applies the rotation, just as the two separate gates do), so the merge unlocks the cheaper synthesis without changing the prepared state.\n"
msgstr "O passe de transpilador [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") detecta o padrão [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") seguido de [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") em um [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") e o reescreve em portas [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"), de modo que uma etapa de síntese posterior aproveita automaticamente a decomposição reduzida. Em simulação, a reescrita não altera o estado: [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") é *validar e depois girar* (ela valida a ocupação de referência e então aplica a rotação, exatamente como as duas portas separadas), então a fusão habilita a síntese mais barata sem alterar o estado preparado.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Throughout this guide, each circuit is drawn before and after the pass, side by side: the input on the left, and the result of running the pass on it on the right. Two helpers do that. `merge` runs the pass on a copy of the circuit (through its [`FermionicDAGCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-dag-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicDAGCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicDAGCircuit\")) and converts the result back to a drawable [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\"), and `draw_merge` draws both halves into a single before/after figure:\n"
msgstr "Ao longo deste guia, cada circuito é desenhado antes e depois do passe, lado a lado: a entrada à esquerda e o resultado da execução do passe sobre ela à direita. Dois auxiliares fazem isso. `merge` executa o passe em uma cópia do circuito (por meio de seu [`FermionicDAGCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-dag-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicDAGCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicDAGCircuit\")) e converte o resultado de volta em um [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") desenhável, e `draw_merge` desenha as duas metades em uma única figura de antes e depois:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What gets merged {#what-gets-merged}"
msgstr "O que é fundido {#what-gets-merged}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The pass recognizes three patterns, all keyed off the block-spin mode convention that [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") and [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") use. For a system with `norb` spatial orbitals, the modes `0..norb` are the spin-alpha sector, and `norb..2*norb` are the spin-beta sector. Slater determinant preparation is done per spin sector because each sector has its own (electrons, orbitals) shape.\n"
msgstr "O passe reconhece três padrões, todos baseados na convenção de modos de spin em blocos que [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") e [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") usam. Para um sistema com `norb` orbitais espaciais, os modos `0..norb` formam o setor de spin alfa e `norb..2*norb` formam o setor de spin beta. A preparação do determinante de Slater é feita por setor de spin, porque cada setor tem seu próprio formato (elétrons, orbitais).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Full-register (or spinless) {#full-register-or-spinless}"
msgstr "Registrador completo (ou sem spin) {#full-register-or-spinless}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simplest pattern is using [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\"), immediately followed by an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") on the *same* modes. This is the spinless case (one determinant over all modes) and also a spinful circuit whose rotation spans both sectors at once. The two gates fuse into a single [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"):\n"
msgstr "O padrão mais simples é usar [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\"), imediatamente seguido de uma [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") nos *mesmos* modos. Este é o caso sem spin (um determinante sobre todos os modos) e também o de um circuito com spin cuja rotação abrange ambos os setores de uma vez. As duas portas se fundem em uma única [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"):\n"

